          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7e616145da8bd8f0eb3019c140dc4cd47e2ddc95",
          "message": "feat(import): flag Pathbuilder feats that fit no slot as rule breaks (#1208)\n\nAn import no longer names a feat no slot offers as \"not offered\". The\ncharacter keeps it in build.unplacedFeats (schema version 11) and the\nrule break is derived on every read (unplacedFeatBreaks), as for the\ninventory. Picking the feat in a slot, or dismissUnplacedFeat, takes it\noff the list.\n\nThe import report counts them (ruleBreakingFeats), the feats tab lists\nthem with Dismiss, and the sheet header counts them with the inventory's\nrule breaks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
