          "distinct": true,
          "id": "82b8a5bcd834499d2a53042dc93e5e349f187f14",
          "message": "feat(campaign): accept or decline an offer (#1279)\n\nThe owner of the recipient character accepts or declines a pending item\nor coin offer (POST /campaigns/:id/transfers/:transferId/accept|decline).\n\nAccepting runs in one database transaction opened in the composition\nroot: the offer must still be pending, the giver must be at the version\nthe offer was made at, and the recipient is written at the version read\nin the transaction. A stale side is a 409 version conflict; a giver who\nlost the line or coins, a key item, or a full recipient is a 409 with a\nmessage key. Characters are written in id order so crossing offers\ncannot deadlock. Declining only marks the offer, leaving the giver as is.\n\nThe pure move lives in the character domain (giveLine, giveCoins) and a\nproperty test shows lines and coins across both characters are\nunchanged. The accept is audited under accept-campaign-transfer and\nacceptTransfer.\n\nCloses #1135\nPart of #274\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:04:20+10:00",
          "tree_id": "7b4a7432f7c8d4eb7465df5ff5a0d5254aa0670b",
